nnection only support the CCID based applications on the YubiKey and does not support U2F, FIDO2 or OTP."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"anchor":"LightningAccessoryConnection-ie-5Ci-YubiKey","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Lightning\/AccessoryConnection i.e 5Ci YubiKey"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To add support for the 5Ci YubiKey that connect to the iPhone via the Lightning port you need to add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.ylp"},{"text":" string to the list of External Accessories.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your project."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your application target."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Choose the “Info” tab.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If not present add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Supported external accessory protocols"},{"text":" key and insert the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.ylp"},{"type":"text","text":" in its list."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"external-accessory.png"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The YubiKey 5Ci is an Apple MFi certified external accessory and communicates over iAP2. Setting the value for ","type":"text"},{"code":"Supported external accessory protocols","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.yubico.ylp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" will tell the app that all communication with the 5Ci YubiKey via the Lightning port is done using the External Accessory framework."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"type":"heading","text":"Making Your First Connection","anchor":"Making-Your-First-Connection","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now that your project is configured, you can start connecting to YubiKeys. YubiKit provides different connection types depending on how the YubiKey is connected to the device.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Understanding Connection Types","anchor":"Understanding-Connection-Types","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"YubiKit handles three different connection methods:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Short-range wireless communication (iOS only)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"USB","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Direct USB connection via SmartCard interface","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lightning"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": YubiKey 5Ci connected to Lightning port (iOS only)","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connection type works differently, so let’s explore how to use them."}]},{"text":"NFC Connections","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"NFC-Connections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC connections are user-initiated and short-lived. The user must bring their YubiKey close to their device:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import YubiKit","","\/\/ Start an NFC scan","do {","    let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","","    \/\/ Use the connection quickly - NFC sessions have a timeout","    let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","    let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","    \/\/ Always close NFC connections with a user message","    await connection.close(message: \"OATH codes retrieved\")","","} catch {","    \/\/ Handle connection errors (user cancelled, no YubiKey found, etc.)","    print(\"NFC connection failed: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC connections automatically show the iOS NFC interface and require user interaction to complete.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"USB and Lightning Connections","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"USB-and-Lightning-Connections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wired connections are persistent - they stay connected until the YubiKey is unplugged:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import YubiKit","","\/\/ Connect to any wired YubiKey (USB or Lightning)","do {","    let connection = try await WiredSmartCardConnection.makeConnection()","","    \/\/ Perform operations - connection stays active","    let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","    let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","    \/\/ Monitor for disconnection or close when done","    let error = await connection.waitUntilClosed()","    if let error = error {","        print(\"Connection closed with error: \\(error)\")","    }","","} catch {","    print(\"Wired connection failed: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"WiredSmartCardConnection.makeConnection()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method automatically detects whether you’re using USB or Lightning.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Specific Connection Types","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Specific-Connection-Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more control, you can connect to specific interfaces:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ USB only","let usbConnection = try await USBSmartCardConnection()","","\/\/ Lightning only (iOS)","let lightningConnection = try await LightningSmartCardConnection()","","\/\/ NFC with custom message (iOS)","let nfcConnection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection(","    alertMessage: \"Hold your YubiKey near the phone\"",")"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Understanding-Connection-Lifecycle","text":"Understanding Connection Lifecycle","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Critical:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Connections must be explicitly closed. You can only have one active connection to a YubiKey at any time.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Connection-Behavior","text":"Connection Behavior","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclusive access"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Only one connection can exist per YubiKey at any time"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Manual closure required"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Dropping a connection reference does NOT automatically close it - you must call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Resource blocking","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": An unclosed connection prevents new connections (throws "},{"code":"SmartCardConnectionError.busy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connection is a lightweight value type that identifies an active hardware session. Copying a connection creates another handle to the same session, not a new connection - the hardware is only released when you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Working with Sessions","anchor":"Working-with-Sessions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you have a connection, create sessions to access different YubiKey applications:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"OATH Session (TOTP\/HOTP codes)","anchor":"OATH-Session-TOTPHOTP-codes","type":"heading"},{"code":["let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","for (credential, code) in codes {","    print(\"\\(credential.label): \\(code?.code ?? \"Touch required\")\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"text":"PIV Session (Certificates and keys)","anchor":"PIV-Session-Certificates-and-keys","type":"heading"},{"code":["let session = try await PIVSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let certificate = try await session.getCertificate(in: .authentication)","print(\"Found certificate: \\(certificate.subject)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"text":"Management Session (Device information)","anchor":"Management-Session-Device-information","type":"heading"},{"code":["let session: Management.Session = try await .makeSession(connection: connection)","print(\"YubiKey version: \\(await session.version)\")","","let deviceInfo = try await session.getDeviceInfo()","print(\"Device info: \\(deviceInfo)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"text":"WebAuthn Client (FIDO2 \/ passkeys)","anchor":"WebAuthn-Client-FIDO2--passkeys","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For passkey registration and authentication, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","type":"reference"},{"text":" wraps a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","type":"reference"},{"text":" and runs the W3C ceremonies end-to-end. CTAP2 sessions can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDFIDOConnection"},{"text":" (USB HID on macOS) or any ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/SmartCardConnection","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(NF